1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,269
Claude's maker is about to go public.

2
00:00:02,319 --> 00:00:07,016
Anthropic plans to start trading on the Nasdaq on the nineteenth of November.

3
00:00:07,066 --> 00:00:12,898
The filing sets a price of seventy to seventy-eight dollars a share, under the ticker A N T.

4
00:00:12,948 --> 00:00:14,487
The growth is huge.

5
00:00:14,537 --> 00:00:22,078
Seventeen billion dollars of revenue in one quarter, and reports say about eighty-one billion in run-rate by the end of October.

6
00:00:22,128 --> 00:00:24,967
Muja, you brought a bell?

7
00:00:25,017 --> 00:00:31,704
Fun fact, buddy: the Dutch East India Company sold shares to the public in Amsterdam in 1602.

8
00:00:31,754 --> 00:00:34,467
It's often called the first big listed company.

9
00:00:34,517 --> 00:00:35,439
Alright...

10
00:00:35,489 --> 00:00:36,908
back to our story.

11
00:00:36,958 --> 00:00:38,744
But the bills are huge too.

12
00:00:38,794 --> 00:00:44,899
Anthropic has committed to about nine hundred billion dollars of future spending, mostly on computing.

13
00:00:44,949 --> 00:00:46,326
Here is what we know.

14
00:00:46,376 --> 00:00:48,505
The price range and the date are set.

15
00:00:48,555 --> 00:00:53,313
The final price isn't, and neither is any change to Claude's prices.

16
00:00:53,363 --> 00:00:54,641
So what should you do?

17
00:00:54,691 --> 00:00:58,895
Yes, Muja, I know, you want cheaper Claude.

18
00:00:58,945 --> 00:01:00,962
But nothing says prices will drop.

19
00:01:01,012 --> 00:01:02,498
So don't assume a cut.

20
00:01:02,548 --> 00:01:05,743
Measure your usage, and keep a second model tested.

21
00:01:05,793 --> 00:01:10,059
My take: watch the margin and the compute costs in the first two reports.

22
00:01:10,109 --> 00:01:12,431
They tell you more than any press release.

23
00:01:12,481 --> 00:01:16,001
Anthropic expects to start trading from the nineteenth of November.

24
00:01:16,051 --> 00:01:18,442
The full story is on my blog.
